 "notes": "Output-only task. The four accepted C++ (3753140, 3753148, 3753205, 3753393) print a table of routes keyed on the test number and assert 1 <= T <= 10, so they crash on the statement sample (T = 0) and answer no other graph; they are no reference and their files are gone. orig.cpp is exact for n <= 20 and for forests and otherwise a deterministic randomized Warnsdorff search with Posa rotations; on the ten official files it matches or beats those tables (10 21 99 500 81 256 1000 200 29 95), and its n <= 10 answers match an exhaustive search on 150 generated graphs. checker.py accepts any valid route at least as long. Bounds come from the official guide1-10.in, since the statement gives none."
